If our operating results fall below the expectations of investors or securities analysts, the price of our common stock could decline
substantially. Furthermore, any fluctuations in our operating results or cash flows may, in turn, cause significant volatility in the price of
our stock. We believe that comparisons of our quarterly financial results are not necessarily meaningful and should not be relied upon as
an indication of our future performance.
Exchange rate fluctuations of foreign currencies relative to the U.S. Dollar could materially and adversely affect our
business.
